<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/peoples-republic-of-china"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/People's%20Republic%20of%20China.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>People's Republic of China</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mao launches the Cultural Revolution</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-buganda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Buganda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Buganda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Troops under Idi Amin storm the kabaka’s palace at Mengo</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/uganda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Uganda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Uganda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Troops under Idi Amin storm the Kabaka’s palace at Mengo</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-burundi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Burundi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Burundi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Michel Micombero deposes Ntare V and proclaims a republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/ban-chiang-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ban%20Chiang%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ban Chiang culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Steve Young finds pottery in a village path, and samples are later sent to the University of Pennsylvania for dating</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/rhodesia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rhodesia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rhodesia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 28 April seven ZANLA insurgents are cornered and killed near Sinoia, the first engagement of the Rhodesian Bush War, kept by ZANU as Chimurenga Day.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/aboriginal-australians"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Aboriginal%20Australians.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Aboriginal Australians</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Wave Hill Walk-Off begins, a strike over working conditions that grows into a claim to the land</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/communism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Communism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Communism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mao’s Cultural Revolution begins, a ten-year upheaval that targets intellectuals and party leaders</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/islamism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Islamism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Islamism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sayyid Qutb is executed for allegedly taking part in a plot to assassinate the president</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Cambodia%20(1953-1970).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Cambodia (1953-1970)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The National Assembly election brings an upsurge in the conservative vote, and General Lon Nol becomes prime minister</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/mao-zedong"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mao%20Zedong.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mao Zedong</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">He launches the Cultural Revolution</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/kwame-nkrumah"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kwame%20Nkrumah.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kwame Nkrumah</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">He is overthrown in a coup while on a state visit to China</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/sukarno"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sukarno.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sukarno</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Under the order known as Supersemar he transfers most presidential authority to Suharto, and he is placed under house arrest the next year</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/surrealism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Surrealism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Surrealism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">André Breton dies, and Surrealist groups continue without him</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/black-consciousness-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Black%20Consciousness%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Black Consciousness Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">An Anglican meeting convened under Archbishop Robert Selby Taylor leads to the University Christian Movement, which becomes the vehicle for Black Consciousness</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/baathism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ba'athism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ba'athism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A second Syrian coup overthrows the old guard led by Aflaq and Bitar and splits the movement into a Syrian and an Iraqi wing</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/african-socialism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/African%20socialism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>African socialism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Senegal's Socialist Party is declared the country's only legal party</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/rastafari"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rastafari.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rastafari</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Haile Selassie visits Jamaica at its government's invitation, and thousands of Rastas gather to see his arrival at the airport</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/potala-palace"><im